WEBVTT

00:01.070 --> 00:03.240
At that point in time, Eyman Prison

00:03.350 --> 00:06.489
was forcing all their death-row
and life-sentence inmates

00:06.490 --> 00:09.450
to take new drugs as part of
clinical trials.

00:09.810 --> 00:13.460
So that means Axel is living proof
of their experiments.

00:13.600 --> 00:15.590
This is going to be our last chance.

00:16.030 --> 00:18.360
Please let me go to Pakistan!

00:19.520 --> 00:21.319
You're aware of the risks, right?

00:21.320 --> 00:22.430
Yes.

00:23.910 --> 00:25.860
Fine, but on one condition.

00:26.290 --> 00:27.190
What?

00:27.650 --> 00:28.900
I'm coming with you.

00:29.170 --> 00:30.010
Got that?

00:31.650 --> 00:32.810
Got it!

00:35.140 --> 00:37.999
The drug they forced you to take
at the Arizona prison

00:38.000 --> 00:39.829
was a prototype of Hapna.

00:39.830 --> 00:40.700
What?

00:40.900 --> 00:44.560
It's very likely that everyone else
who took it is already dead.

00:45.060 --> 00:46.170
Seriously?

00:46.400 --> 00:50.020
[Hersch Lindemann]

00:46.670 --> 00:48.949
You escaped right after
the clinical trial ended,

00:48.950 --> 00:51.080
so you obviously had no way of knowing,

00:51.520 --> 00:53.229
but the only involved person
who's still alive

00:53.230 --> 00:55.419
is the prison doctor that served there.

00:55.420 --> 00:56.489
Do you remember him?

00:56.490 --> 00:58.220
Sure do. I know him well.

01:03.340 --> 01:06.240
I need you to go and ensure
his safety immediately.

01:06.490 --> 01:07.560
Got it.

01:07.730 --> 01:08.890
But how in the hell

01:09.440 --> 01:11.320
am I the only one still alive?

01:26.760 --> 01:28.990
[37.7°C]

01:28.690 --> 01:29.520
Eleina.

01:29.770 --> 01:30.769
Everything okay?

01:30.770 --> 01:32.110
Oh, yeah.

01:32.240 --> 01:33.370
I'm alright.

03:08.800 --> 03:14.740
[LAZARUS]

03:31.100 --> 03:35.950
[Islamabad Airport, Pakistan]

03:43.090 --> 03:44.710
What's Popcorn's location?

03:45.120 --> 03:48.180
33.693578.

03:48.740 --> 03:50.770
Same as it was seven hours ago.

03:50.890 --> 03:51.890
Okay.

03:51.990 --> 03:52.979
But...

03:52.980 --> 03:54.999
maybe she'll move again,

03:55.000 --> 03:56.770
just like at Delta Medicinal.

03:58.170 --> 03:59.870
Your face is really red.

04:00.050 --> 04:00.870
Eh?

04:00.990 --> 04:02.430
Are you running a fever?

04:03.810 --> 04:05.600
It could be a symptom of Hapna.

04:06.410 --> 04:07.600
Fever...

04:09.450 --> 04:10.550
I'm okay.

04:10.640 --> 04:12.740
[38.3°C]

04:11.200 --> 04:12.200
I see.

04:12.990 --> 04:14.860
She's moving.

04:15.200 --> 04:16.380
Perfect timing.

04:16.510 --> 04:18.910
No matter where she goes,
we'll follow her.

04:23.760 --> 04:24.850
When was that?

04:26.510 --> 04:28.830
I understand. Thank you.

04:30.060 --> 04:32.369
A special operations aircraft
out of Fort Belvoir

04:32.370 --> 04:34.179
has departed for Pakistan.

04:34.180 --> 04:35.449
Fort?

04:35.450 --> 04:38.100
That's the INSCOM.

04:38.220 --> 04:39.900
Pakistan...

04:40.170 --> 04:42.200
You mean just like Doug and Eleina?

04:42.360 --> 04:44.740
Is the Army tracking them?

04:44.880 --> 04:46.280
I'm afraid so.

04:46.700 --> 04:48.599
We're starting to get close to something

04:48.600 --> 04:50.658
they really don't want us to find out.

04:50.659 --> 04:52.210
That much is certain.

04:52.800 --> 04:55.408
There's no time. I need to
contact them directly.

04:55.409 --> 04:58.010
You mean contact the Army directly?

04:58.380 --> 04:59.610
Do me a favor.

05:00.080 --> 05:03.340
Give this letter to the man who will be
visiting here later.

05:03.540 --> 05:04.920
Ah, okay.

05:06.360 --> 05:07.840
So, what man?

05:08.210 --> 05:09.180
No idea.

05:17.900 --> 05:19.420
What the hell?

05:20.750 --> 05:22.530
As fierce as fire in attack;

05:23.690 --> 05:25.620
as steady as a mountain in defense.

05:56.980 --> 05:57.989
Come on, man.

05:57.990 --> 05:59.540
I don't even get a hello.

06:19.880 --> 06:21.640
Come and get me!

06:32.310 --> 06:34.310
Trigger-happy bastard.

07:06.060 --> 07:08.700
Okay, I'll admit it. You're not half bad.

07:11.410 --> 07:15.230
[Episode 11: Runnin' with the Devil]

07:16.190 --> 07:18.540
[US Army INSCOM]

07:17.190 --> 07:18.590
I'm Hersch Lindemann.

07:18.900 --> 07:21.030
I'm here to see Lieutenant Schneider.

07:21.150 --> 07:22.679
Do you have an appointment?

07:22.680 --> 07:25.870
Nobody calls ahead when they're coming to start a fight.

07:27.430 --> 07:28.960
Where's Hersch?

07:29.390 --> 07:31.139
I can't reach her.

07:31.140 --> 07:33.559
She said she went to the Army.

07:33.560 --> 07:34.590
Army?

07:34.730 --> 07:36.740
INSCOM?

07:36.990 --> 07:39.180
She asked me to give this to you.

07:39.740 --> 07:40.839
By the way,

07:40.840 --> 07:42.109
who are you?

07:42.110 --> 07:44.030
Ah, sorry.

07:44.240 --> 07:46.200
I'm Abel Anderson,

07:46.590 --> 07:48.310
the founder of Lazarus.

07:49.770 --> 07:50.810
Do you know him?

07:51.050 --> 07:52.010
Yes.

08:35.400 --> 08:39.470
[NSA Headquarters]

08:36.370 --> 08:37.190
Eh?

08:37.559 --> 08:38.579
No way.

08:38.580 --> 08:39.580
What is this?

08:41.970 --> 08:43.250
What happened?

08:49.510 --> 08:52.990
What? Didn't you come to kill me?

08:53.260 --> 08:56.160
If you don't hurry, I'll get away again.

09:05.020 --> 09:07.150
The same tricks won't work on me twice!

09:16.080 --> 09:17.829
Oh, my.

09:17.830 --> 09:20.690
Sorry for making you come all the way here.

09:21.240 --> 09:22.970
I hate beating around the bush,

09:23.530 --> 09:25.650
so I'll cut to the chase.

09:27.650 --> 09:30.399
Please stop tracking my subordinates

09:30.400 --> 09:31.940
in Pakistan.

09:33.130 --> 09:35.360
Pakistan?

09:35.790 --> 09:36.920
If not,

09:37.220 --> 09:38.529
I'll reveal all the information

09:38.530 --> 09:40.400
I know related to you people.

09:40.930 --> 09:44.490
What do you mean by "information related to us"?

09:45.080 --> 09:46.380
Eyman Prison.

09:48.190 --> 09:49.580
Axel Gilberto.

09:51.100 --> 09:52.580
Is this a guessing game?

09:53.050 --> 09:55.100
If so, I'm gonna need more clues.

09:55.700 --> 09:57.699
It's not that there aren't enough clues—

09:57.700 --> 09:59.629
it's the number of corpses, right?

09:59.630 --> 10:01.719
INSCOM

10:01.720 --> 10:03.039
secretly conducted clinical trials

10:03.040 --> 10:06.640
of new drugs on death row inmates

10:06.970 --> 10:09.520
and lifers at Eyman Prison.

10:10.190 --> 10:12.290
All test subjects died.

10:12.590 --> 10:15.590
Of course, there are no official records.

10:16.260 --> 10:17.790
The only giveaway

10:18.400 --> 10:20.200
was a missing body.

10:21.010 --> 10:23.540
Looks like someone survived
that experiment

10:23.710 --> 10:25.640
and even managed to escape prison.

10:26.420 --> 10:29.210
That would be Mr. Gilberto, right?

10:32.710 --> 10:34.740
Well, I'm a little shocked.

10:34.920 --> 10:38.870
I can't believe that the NSA was fooled
by such fake information.

10:39.470 --> 10:41.989
You still think like one of
the subordinates,

10:41.990 --> 10:43.110
Ms. Hersch.

10:43.750 --> 10:47.450
I hope Axel Gilberto can live a long life.

10:48.940 --> 10:50.000
I see.

10:50.560 --> 10:51.469
While the whole world

10:51.470 --> 10:53.800
is desperately searching for Skinner,

10:54.230 --> 10:56.910
you have ulterior motives.

10:58.590 --> 11:00.010
I'll say it one more time—

11:00.340 --> 11:03.039
please stop tracking my subordinates

11:03.040 --> 11:04.530
in Pakistan immediately.

11:05.790 --> 11:07.500
I'm so sorry,

11:07.860 --> 11:11.610
but you'll be staying here for a while.

11:12.200 --> 11:14.000
Your charge would be...

11:14.510 --> 11:16.930
well, treason or something like that.

11:20.050 --> 11:21.989
So, you've finally shown your true colors,

11:21.990 --> 11:23.390
Lieutenant Schneider.

11:25.550 --> 11:27.100
What a pity.

11:29.210 --> 11:30.139
Alas.

11:30.140 --> 11:32.280
Truly reckless and unwise.

11:32.440 --> 11:33.930
What does it say?

11:34.590 --> 11:38.530
Hersch has probably been detained
by INSCOM.

11:38.710 --> 11:39.709
What?

11:39.710 --> 11:40.639
She went to negotiate,

11:40.640 --> 11:43.450
demanding they stop tracking them
in Pakistan.

11:44.000 --> 11:47.059
No word from her since, and she hasn't
returned either.

11:47.060 --> 11:49.550
That means the negotiation failed.

11:49.840 --> 11:50.819
How could that be?

11:50.820 --> 11:52.510
Then, what about Hersch?

11:53.790 --> 11:55.120
Liz, what's wrong?

11:55.550 --> 11:56.589
Listen carefully.

11:56.590 --> 11:59.790
There's been a string of explosions
throughout the city.

12:00.010 --> 12:02.130
There are two men in the center

12:02.270 --> 12:03.579
of the chaos.

12:03.580 --> 12:07.400
[Liz]

12:04.180 --> 12:05.980
I'm sending you the footage now.

12:07.630 --> 12:09.109
[Camera 16]

12:09.110 --> 12:10.109
Axel?

12:10.110 --> 12:10.829
Eh?

12:10.830 --> 12:13.049
Wasn't he supposed to go to
the Witness Protection Center?

12:13.050 --> 12:14.260
Who's the other guy?

12:14.510 --> 12:17.890
Probably a hitman hired by the Army.

12:18.560 --> 12:19.580
And

12:19.700 --> 12:21.219
even the NSA database

12:21.220 --> 12:23.010
has no record of that man.

12:21.380 --> 12:23.350
[No Match]

12:23.750 --> 12:25.420
This man...

12:26.790 --> 12:27.820
Could he be...

12:28.410 --> 12:32.110
The Phantom Assassin has appeared?

12:33.490 --> 12:42.370
[LAZARUS]

12:47.750 --> 12:49.680
How long until we reach the target?

12:50.200 --> 12:52.060
22 more minutes.

12:52.530 --> 12:53.520
Eleina,

12:53.770 --> 12:56.969
if we find Skinner and peace is finally
restored to the world,

12:56.970 --> 12:58.339
what's the first thing you want to do?

12:58.340 --> 12:59.309
What?

12:59.310 --> 13:01.710
Even if it's something small, just say it.

13:02.500 --> 13:03.820
Well...

13:04.210 --> 13:07.319
Ah, I want to eat a McDonald's Big Mac.

13:07.320 --> 13:08.890
Oh, you like them?

13:09.050 --> 13:11.290
No way. They are disgusting.

13:12.060 --> 13:15.500
But sometimes, I get a strong craving
for one.

13:16.300 --> 13:18.110
I like them.

13:18.560 --> 13:20.000
I'm sorry.

13:21.640 --> 13:23.569
They've been following us all this time.

13:23.570 --> 13:24.500
What?

13:24.890 --> 13:26.500
I'll take care of this.

13:26.810 --> 13:29.340
Can you make it to where Popcorn is
on your own?

13:31.460 --> 13:32.450
But...

13:32.610 --> 13:36.360
You're the only one who can find
Skinner's location right now.

13:38.800 --> 13:41.660
Sometimes I have to show others
my good side, right?

13:44.610 --> 13:47.030
No, I didn't mean I'd sacrifice myself.

13:47.280 --> 13:49.830
I'm just going to surrender
and hold them off.

13:50.240 --> 13:52.110
Oh, okay.

13:58.820 --> 14:00.360
I've heard the rumors.

14:01.130 --> 14:06.200
No one has ever seen
the Phantom Assassin and lived.

14:06.710 --> 14:07.599
Maybe

14:07.600 --> 14:10.159
the one who wiped out

14:10.160 --> 14:11.680
an entire unit of INSCOM

14:11.860 --> 14:13.129
was also this man.

14:13.130 --> 14:15.249
Can you give me permission
to use an assault rifle?

14:15.250 --> 14:16.599
You can use anything.

14:16.600 --> 14:17.439
Um...

14:17.440 --> 14:18.689
I'm coming too.

14:18.690 --> 14:19.729
Leland,

14:19.730 --> 14:21.610
you have to stay here.

14:21.750 --> 14:24.390
We might all need to return here.

14:22.730 --> 14:31.380
[No Match]

14:25.540 --> 14:27.830
I'm going to save Hersch.

14:28.190 --> 14:30.240
I'm counting on you here, Leland.

14:30.550 --> 14:31.510
Okay.

14:32.160 --> 14:33.300
Chris!

14:34.550 --> 14:35.780
Please...

14:36.360 --> 14:38.070
you must bring Axel back.

14:39.370 --> 14:40.510
I know.

15:04.760 --> 15:06.209
The other guy isn't in the car.

15:06.210 --> 15:07.390
You bastard!

15:10.140 --> 15:11.200
Humph.

16:08.910 --> 16:10.120
Why are you smiling?

16:10.620 --> 16:12.910
Aren't you afraid of death?

16:13.810 --> 16:16.880
I've come close to death many times.

16:17.270 --> 16:19.910
It already feels like an old friend to me.

16:20.660 --> 16:22.530
You're just like me, aren't you?

16:32.140 --> 16:33.230
Axel.

16:45.130 --> 16:47.260
It's... over there.

17:00.570 --> 17:01.600
Wait...

17:12.650 --> 17:13.760
Wait...

17:19.200 --> 17:20.369
That's it.

17:23.319 --> 17:24.420
Wait!

17:46.830 --> 17:47.970
Huh?

17:48.420 --> 17:50.360
Mad Screamer?

17:57.310 --> 17:58.610
What the hell?

18:34.370 --> 18:35.730
Looks like...

18:35.940 --> 18:38.800
this isn't ending until one of us is dead.

18:40.760 --> 18:42.100
What's wrong?

18:42.200 --> 18:44.800
Dibs on the first move,
if you're not taking it.

19:09.910 --> 19:13.990
[Hundun]

19:11.500 --> 19:12.560
Yes.

19:13.160 --> 19:14.600
Abandon your heart

19:15.550 --> 19:18.300
and become a monster with no expression.

19:24.300 --> 19:26.630
The Wings of Hundun...

19:27.260 --> 19:28.400
Huh?

19:41.980 --> 19:43.550
Who are you?

19:44.420 --> 19:45.970
No one.

19:46.550 --> 19:48.020
Who are you?

19:48.530 --> 19:49.980
No one.

19:50.340 --> 19:52.000
Who are you?

20:00.190 --> 20:03.980
[Hundun]

20:03.270 --> 20:06.810
People who felt sorry for Hundun
having no expression

20:07.960 --> 20:10.330
carved a hole into his face.

20:08.170 --> 20:11.400
[Hundun]

20:12.410 --> 20:14.940
But Hundun was in great pain.

20:14.620 --> 20:16.940
[Hundun]

20:16.120 --> 20:18.920
So he went berserk, and there was no way
to stop him.

20:22.410 --> 20:23.530
And then...

20:38.420 --> 20:40.070
Abandon your emotions.

20:41.520 --> 20:43.200
Abandon your reasoning.

20:43.760 --> 20:45.160
Abandon your heart.

20:55.320 --> 20:56.260
Right.

20:57.100 --> 21:00.430
You will all become monsters
without expressions.

21:30.430 --> 21:31.960
I can't remember.

21:36.200 --> 21:37.570
Tell me.

21:38.370 --> 21:41.750
After Hundun had a hole drilled
into his face,

21:44.850 --> 21:47.520
what happened after that?

22:05.730 --> 22:06.840
Axel.

22:09.640 --> 22:10.890
Axel!

22:15.570 --> 22:17.370
[5 Days Left...]

23:49.890 --> 23:54.800
[Next Episode] [#12 Close to the Edge]
